# Alertmanager delivers Prometheus alerts to the ops Telegram chat — the same
# one the bot already posts fulfilment failures to, deliberately: an alert in a
# channel nobody has open is the failure this service exists to fix.
#
# Reuse the values already in api.env:
#   ALERT_BOT_TOKEN  <- TG_ALERT_BOT_TOKEN
#   ALERT_CHAT_ID    <- TG_ALERT_CHAT_ID
#
# TG_ALERT_BOT_TOKEN specifically, not the storefront or admin bot. Ops alerts
# run on their own bot on purpose (see notifications/alerts.py) so a leak of one
# token does not reach the others — and, practically, that is the bot which is
# actually a member of the alert chat. Another bot's token authenticates fine
# and then fails to post, which looks identical to no alerts at all.
#
# Both are substituted into the config at container start-up; Alertmanager does
# no environment expansion of its own.
ALERT_BOT_TOKEN=
ALERT_CHAT_ID=
